    "text": "<p>Cobalt salts are pink in anhydrous & blue in hydrated form<br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/2_solu_chem_pa1.jpg\"/></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/2_solu_chem_pa1_2.jpg\"/></p><p>(i)  Hybridisation of (Y) is <math><msup><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> as <math><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3 </mn></mrow></msub></math>is a strong field ligand</p><p>(ii)  <math><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> have <math><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> hybridisation as <math><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> is a weak field ligand</p><p>(iii)   <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/2_solu_chem_pa1_333.jpg\"/></p><p>(iv)  <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/2_solu_chem_pa1_4_1.jpg\"/></p>",
